Hi Mike,

I've just started playing for the first time with the container model in ectotherm(), which has been cool for predicting e.g. changes in water levels over time. I'm now trying to explore ectothermic development with the container model on (ultimately for frogs, but for now just to understand what's going on).

I'm finding some seemingly strange behavior to DEB outputs when the container model is running. For example, attached is a script that pulls entirely from the DEB model vignette <https://48b294cf.streaklinks.com/CIiRi51DA-Ptu5Yh0APq42Nc/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmrke%2FNicheMapR%2Fblob%2Fmaster%2Fvignettes%2Fectotherm-model-tutorial.Rmd> (and as such draws from AddMyPet allstat.rda <https://48b294cf.streaklinks.com/CIiRi51o6AfN72NnTgFCGcl-/https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bio.vu.nl%2Fthb%2Fdeb%2Fdeblab%2Fadd_my_pet%2FAmPdata%2FAmPdata.zip>), but at the bottom I run ectotherm() twice: once with the container model off, and again with it on. It seems the predicted wetmass is constant at 50 g (even though Ww_g is left at default of 40, and all initial conditions for DEB left as-is), and the organism never develops beyond the first stage. The content from the DEB vignette wasn't meant to use the container model, but for this example I thought better to stick with content from the DEB vignette than to tweak further.

Any guesses why I'm finding this? I dug through the archives of the Google Group, and looked back at the papers, and although there's some useful content on using the container model for predicting water temperatures (eg here <https://48b294cf.streaklinks.com/CIiRi5xs7CH2buYIOgpfjQ76/https%3A%2F%2Fgroups.google.com%2Fg%2Fnichemapr%2Fc%2Fl_QOFUFRNDo%2Fm%2F6Xv9lzmFAgAJ> on Google Group), I haven't found too much (yet) to help guide me on how the container model influences the DEB outputs. Closest papers seem to be Kearney et al. 2009 Functional Ecology <https://48b294cf.streaklinks.com/CIiRi512dim6ghoLLwFzS-dU/https%3A%2F%2Fbesjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com%2Fdoi%2Ffull%2F10.1111%2Fj.1365-2435.2008.01538.x>, and Urtzi's 2019 GCB paper <https://48b294cf.streaklinks.com/CIiRi51i4l6cTsrPCAmlkh60/https%3A%2F%2Fonlinelibrary.wiley.com%2Fdoi%2Ffull%2F10.1111%2Fgcb.14673%3Fcasa_token%3DhMXVBmA4CxAAAAAA%253AxDTGXgUeKBuE61-fJg3OCwd--Ul0XXPYJXvArTV4QpGDFO8mG5gPDaR2wxI654AA2O0W3wBSAufn-1fy> is relevant although I don't think he ran the container model.

Thanks!
Dave

